/14#issuecomment-4136620092"},"message":"## Routing fix: gabby → operator network via WiFi bridge\n\n### Problem\nGabby (192.168.20.5) could not reach hosts on the operator network (192.168.13.0/24) — pings to `salmon.op.p11.lan` and `deadpool.op.p11.lan` had 100% packet loss. The VPN NETMAP addresses (192.168.22.x) worked but routed through the VPN tunnel (~37ms).\n\n### Root cause\nBizzyBoat's router (RUTX11) had no static route for 192.168.13.0/24. Traffic to the operator subnet fell through to the default route (cellular/wlan) instead of going through the WiFi bridge to the operator router at 172.16.20.2.\n\n### Fix\nAdded two static routes on BizzyBoat's router via the web UI:\n\n| Target | Netmask | Gateway | Path |\n|--------|---------|---------|------|\n| 192.168.13.0 | 255.255.255.0 | 172.16.20.2 | WiFi bridge → operator LAN |\n| 192.168.12.0 | 255.255.255.0 | 172.16.20.2 | WiFi bridge → IzzyBoat LAN |\n\nThe operator router already had the return route (`192.168.20.0/24 via 172.16.20.1`), so no changes were needed there.\n\n### Verification\nFrom gabby after the fix:\n- `ping -c 1 deadpool.op.p11.lan` → 1.85ms ✓\n- `ping -c 1 salmon.op.p11.lan` → 3.05ms ✓\n- `ping -c 1 salmon.vpn.bizzy.p11.lan` → 36.7ms ✓ (VPN path still works too)\n\n### Notes\n- `deadpool.vpn.bizzy.p11.lan` is missing from the hosts file (only salmon has a VPN NETMAP entry) — not yet added.\n- ZeroTier on gabby is planned for later; gitcloud is not yet reachable from gabby.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1774652060,"nonce":"ZjIj2amx+mzPRwtHfIjYLzx+nnI=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM73G8JX","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/14#issuecomment-4145791575"},"message":"## Status Update — 2026-03-27\n\n### Critical Path — ALL COMPLETE\n\n| # | Task | Status |\n|---|------|--------|\n| [ros2_agent_workspace#422](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_agent_workspace/issues/422) |